// docs/08 §2.5 pilot-gate ground truth.
//
// One line per photograph. This file is the LABELS, and it is the part of the
// gate that cannot be automated: someone has to look at each photograph and say
// what it is, before the model does, or the gate is the model grading itself.
//
// Fields:
//   category             exactly one of closet/mapper.ts's CATEGORIES
//   subcategoryKeywords  every one must appear in the returned subcategory
//   primaryColor         head nouns, ANY of which counts as right
//   pattern              acceptable values, more than one where genuinely ambiguous
//   formality            0-100 per docs/05 §3's anchor table; scored within ±15
//
// Listing several acceptable answers is not the same as lowering the bar. A
// chenille shirt is defensibly `solid` and defensibly `texture-only`; marking
// one of them wrong would measure the labeller's preference, not the model.
//
// CURRENT SAMPLE: 1 photograph. That is not a pilot sample and this gate does
// not pretend otherwise — with n=1 an accuracy figure is a coin flip and the
// numbers below are a smoke test of the harness. §2.5 asks for a labeled sample
// of real consented user-scan photos; supplying it is the outstanding work.
